      "writtenOn": "2024-08-02T23:53:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done, but right now these provider callbacks live for ever.\n\nWe can provide a removeAccessorProvider, but it would require the caller having some sort of handle to know which one to remove.\n\nWhat can that handle be? The address of the ARpc_AccessorProvider function they pass in is an option, but I imagine we want to support being able to register multiple providers with the same function pointer but different data pointers.\n\nMaybe a unique string to name the provider? That could lead to collision between two different libraries in one process. I think I like using the ARpc_AccessorProvider ptr more than this. I think it\u0027s unlikely that a library will want to reuse the same provider function with different data as that provider should be able to service all instances it knows about.",
      "parentUuid": "f430d958_93e40f80",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 72,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 72,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "3ea0d97a6f62aed0f659e0046f074ffc9e080cf3",
