      "writtenOn": "2024-07-23T22:54:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: ARpc_Accessor isn\u0027t really nothing at all (it\u0027s a pointer to a binder). Could it be the binder object directly instead?\n\nThat is:\n```\nusing ARpc_Accessor \u003d IAccessor;\n```\n\nThat way, if you get the same accessor out, you\u0027ll have pointer equality for it. Also, you can recover the LocalAccessor if it is a local object.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 107,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 107,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "3ea0d97a6f62aed0f659e0046f074ffc9e080cf3",
