        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 107,
      "author": {
        "id": 1644679
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-02T23:53:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we might need to do this (and attach callbacks to the binder itself) to handle the case where we send the binder out of the process and libbinder holds a strong ref to it. In that case (and in the future case where libbinder delegates and registers with service manager) I think ARpc_Accessor_delete is not going to be able to delete anything useful. Am I thinking about this correctly?\n\nI\u0027m concerned specifically about the `void* data` that we pass to ARpc_Accessor_new along with the `ARpc_ConnectionInfoProviderUserData_delete` callback that should be responsible for deleting it. `ARpc_ConnectionInfoProviderUserData_delete` can\u0027t be called if the IAccessor implementation is still holding the std::function that has captured `void* data`.",
      "parentUuid": "3179b133_c91f4356",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 107,
        "startChar": 33,
        "endLine": 107,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "3ea0d97a6f62aed0f659e0046f074ffc9e080cf3",
